\series default
\end_layout

\begin_layout Exercise*
A constant-returns technology is 
\begin_inset Formula $Q=A[\alpha K^{-\rho}+(1-\alpha)\ell^{-\rho}]^{-1/\rho}$
\end_inset
, with 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho>-1$
\end_inset
 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho\ne0$
\end_inset
. A strictly positive interior cost-minimizing benchmark observation gives 
\begin_inset Formula $(Q,K,\ell,r,W)$
\end_inset
 and an elasticity of substitution 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma>0$
\end_inset
, 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma\ne1$
\end_inset
. (The Cobb-Douglas limit 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma=1$
\end_inset
 is outside the displayed parameterization.)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Exercise*
(a) Recover 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho$
\end_inset
 from 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma$
\end_inset
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Exercise*
(b) Use the cost-minimizing first-order condition to recover 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha$
\end_inset
.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Exercise*
