\begin_layout Exercise*
A small open economy takes the world price 
\begin_inset Formula $P^{W}$
\end_inset
 and exchange rate 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathrm{ER}$
\end_inset
 as given. A tariff 
\begin_inset Formula $\tau$
\end_inset
 implies domestic price 
\begin_inset Formula $P=\mathrm{ER}\,P^{W}(1+\tau)$
\end_inset
. Let differentiable domestic demand and supply be 
\begin_inset Formula $D(P)$
\end_inset
 and 
\begin_inset Formula $S(P)$
\end_inset
, imports be 
\begin_inset Formula $M(P)=D(P)-S(P)>0$
\end_inset
, and tariff revenue be returned lump-sum, 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathrm{TR}(\tau)=\tau\,\mathrm{ER}\,P^{W}M(P(\tau))$
\end_inset
. Interpret 
